# ── Gonka's MC Nations ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is the PACK and nothing else: configs, scripts, and the mod
# manifest — what someone needs to rebuild and run this exact build.
#
# It deliberately does not track worlds, caches, logs, third-party mod
# jars, or documentation. Design notes, planning and write-ups stay off
# GitHub entirely; see /docs/ below.

# ── Documentation and design notes stay out of the repo ──
# Not secret, just not what this repo is for. Keep them local.
/docs/
/*.md
!/README.md
/notes/

# CHANGELOG.md is the exception, and deliberately so: it is the only doc written for
# players rather than for us. scripts/release.py uses the matching section as the
# GitHub release notes, so it has to be in the repo at the tag it describes, or the
# release that quotes it cannot be reconstructed later.
!/CHANGELOG.md
# CLAUDE.md is repo mechanics, not design notes: how to edit files here without
# flipping line endings, where the version lives, why the ledger is append-only.
# A clone needs it; docs/ stays local on purpose, this does not.
# CLAUDE.md is NOT tracked: GitHub carries the pack and the tooling to build it,
# not documentation and not AI instructions. The file stays on this machine, the
# same way docs/ does.
/CLAUDE.md

# ── This machine's view of the live server ──
# Holds the server address and the FTP account name. Never tracked; the example beside
# it is. See scripts/release-local.example.json.
/scripts/release-local.json

# ── Worlds and per-world data ──
/minecraft/saves/
/minecraft/Distant_Horizons_server_data/
/minecraft/server-resource-packs/

# ── Generated caches and build noise ──
/minecraft/.mixin.out/
/minecraft/.probe/
/minecraft/.sable/
/minecraft/.vscode/
/minecraft/dynamic-data-pack-cache/
/minecraft/dynamic-resource-pack-cache/
/minecraft/downloads/
/minecraft/coremods/
/minecraft/texturepacks/

# ── Logs, crashes, debug dumps ──
/minecraft/logs/
/minecraft/crash-reports/
/minecraft/debug/
/minecraft/screenshots/
/minecraft/bluemap/logs/

# ── Per-world / per-server state (the JEI path embeds the server IP) ──
/minecraft/config/jei/world/
/minecraft/bluemap/pluginState.json

# ── Per-player state, not pack content ──
/minecraft/xaero/
# Carried over from the old 1.21.1 instance. The gonk pack's .gitignore had this line
# and this one did not, so it was the single file the new preflight gate flagged as
# neither tracked nor ignored. build-client-package.py already kept it out of the zip.
/minecraft/XaeroWaypoints_BACKUP240807/
/minecraft/usercache.json
/minecraft/usernamecache.json
/minecraft/patchouli_data.json
/minecraft/patchouli_books/
/minecraft/ponders_watched.json
/minecraft/command_history.txt

# ── Contains the live server address ──
/minecraft/servers.dat
/minecraft/servers.dat_old

# ── Contains a generated auth token ──
/minecraft/kubejs/config/web_server.json

# Resourceful Config's web server: holds a generated password for its local web UI,
# one per machine. build-client-package.py already excluded it from the player zip,
# but nothing kept it out of git — check-no-secrets.sh caught it on the commit that
# first tracked the config tree, which is exactly the commit it would have gone
# public in. Each install generates its own.
/minecraft/config/resourceful-config-web.json

# Structurize's local scan pack: per-player state named after whoever scanned, not
# pack content. The pack's own blueprints ship inside the thee jar at
# blueprints/thee/gonk/, discovered by Structurize straight out of it.
/minecraft/blueprints/

# ── Mod jars: track the packwiz index, not the downloads ──
# mods/.index/*.pw.toml carries the URL + sha512 for every mod that
# Prism installed, so third-party jars are reproducible without being
# redistributed here. The exceptions below are added by hand and have
# no index entry, so they must be tracked or the pack won't build.
#
# These are version globs on purpose. Exact filenames meant that
# shipping thee-1.0.1.jar would silently drop the pack's own mod from
# the repo. Match the name, not the version.
/minecraft/mods/*
!/minecraft/mods/.index/

# the checksum manifest for the jars below — without this line the guard
# against a wrong hand-installed build silently never reaches the repo
!/minecraft/mods/hand-installed.sha1

# the append-only record of every version of a pack-built mod and the sha1 it had.
# hand-installed.sha1 pins the jar that is in mods/ right now, which cannot catch a
# rebuild at an unchanged version — the manifest just gets updated too. The ledger is
# the part that remembers, so it has to survive a clone.
!/minecraft/mods/version-ledger.tsv

# custom, unreproducible — losing these loses the pack
!/minecraft/mods/thee-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/chaosgate-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/omnifix-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/atlas-*.jar

# third-party, hand-installed (no packwiz index entry)
!/minecraft/mods/kubejs-neoforge-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/kubejs-create-neoforge-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/lootjs-neoforge-*.jar
!/minecraft/mods/morejs-neoforge-*.jar

# A vendored loader installer: 7 MB, reproducible from maven, no business in git.
/scripts/.vendor/

# Python bytecode from the release scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# built player zip - 550 MB, rebuild with scripts/build-client-package.py
dist/

# ---- 2026-11-21 mod intake -------------------------------------------------
# Nineteen jars that arrived as a player's mods folder, with no CurseForge or
# Modrinth provenance to put in the packwiz index. Tracked directly instead, on
# the same reasoning as the kubejs set above: a jar nobody can reproduce from an
# index has to live in the repo or a fresh clone silently installs a smaller pack
# than the one we ship. hand-installed.sha1 pins every one of them.
!/minecraft/mods/backbone-neoforge-1.2.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/BrewinAndChewin-neoforge-4.5.0+1.21.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/cirrus-neoforge-1.21.1-1.4.2.jar
!/minecraft/mods/diegesis-neoforge-1.21.1-1.0.0-beta.15.jar
!/minecraft/mods/eatinganimation-1.21.0-6.0.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/exposure-neoforge-1.21.1-1.9.21.jar
!/minecraft/mods/gml-6.0.2.jar
!/minecraft/mods/handson_delight-neoforge-1.21.1-1.6.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/icys-better-horses-2.1.8-neo-1.21.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/let_it_walk-0.1.5.jar
!/minecraft/mods/modonomicon-1.21.1-neoforge-1.123.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/MouseTweaks-neoforge-mc1.21-2.26.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/octo-arms-1.8.0+mc1.21.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/particular-1.21.1-NeoForge-1.6.1.jar
# places is 122 MB, over GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, so it CANNOT be tracked
# here however much we want the repo to be self-contained - a push carrying it is
# rejected outright. It stays pinned in hand-installed.sha1 so the local copy is still
# verified; a fresh clone has to fetch this one jar by hand until it gets a packwiz entry.
# /minecraft/mods/places-0.5.5-neoforge-1.21.1.jar  (deliberately NOT un-ignored)
!/minecraft/mods/places_sable-1.0.0-neoforge-1.21.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/the_beyond-1.0.1.jar
!/minecraft/mods/weatherglass-0.6.2-1.21.1-neoforge.jar
!/minecraft/mods/yet_another_config_lib_v3-3.8.2+1.21.1-neoforge.jar

minecraft/particular_cache/
